@kimmonismus yeah tried this last night when building something and it actually worked. 

i tried several times to ask for exactly what i wanted, it was producing a good result but not to my specs 

then in my next prompt, i copy-pasted it twice in the same message and the result was spot on

@paul_cal @kimmonismus Yep, matches my experience. 

Bring the main topic first, then the context, so it's prepared to answer.

That's why system prompts exist and work generally well.

@kimmonismus ⚠️ It's very important to note: this is for non-reasoning models.

For models that are reasoning/thinking, this trick isn't needed.

That being said, it's a very helpful tip for non-reasoning models.

before everyone starts copy-pasting their prompts twice:

@paul_cal already showed this is mostly explained by putting the question first instead of last. the "repeat everything" framing is clickbait.

the real takeaway: prompt structure matters more than prompt length. put important stuff where the model can use it.

@kimmonismus “Don’t make me tell you twice!”

It all comes full circle. 

We’ve created ourselves.

